  "unread": [
    "The drawing names no connector (P1 used).",
    "The letter-side mates of pins 1, 20, 19, 18, 22 and of the letter-only controls are not shown, so it is not known whether they are strapped.",
    "Whether the crosspoint control contacts are active-low closures or voltages is not stated."
  ],
  "confidence": "medium",
  "notes": "System interconnection drawing (size D, DRN MRW 1/79, ENG MRW), not a connector table: M712B pin numbers are read from the labels at each module symbol. Each M712B has 12 lamp-symbol crosspoints: matrix inputs 1-12 on 6,F 7,H 8,J 9,K 10,L 11,M 12,N 13,P 14,R 15,S 16,T 17,U (number and letter given together, i.e. both contacts), each switched by a control line on E, D, C, 5, 4, 3, X, W, V, 20, 19, 18 respectively (control -> input order as drawn left to right). Amplifier output 2,B; +25V on 1; ground 22. Modules cascade: each output feeds the next module's 21,Y through 2 x 27K, the last module's 2,B gives the typical headset output +8dBm nom. Inputs 13 / 14 ... N-11 ... N are looped to other buses; controls form the matrix controls. Also on the sheet (other modules, not recorded as pins here): M701B mic amp (typ. mic input DYN -75 to -45dBm 150 ohm / CARBON -25 to +5dBm 150 ohm on 3,4 and 5; output 8,J via 620 ohm at +8dBm; +25V 1; ground 10; remote DYN/CARBON select K) and M702B output amp (input U,V and T; +32V 13,P; balanced output W,X +8dBm 600 ohm; unbalanced output 21&Y, 22&Z 8 ohm 3W max; part mute 18, mute 19, mute override 20)."
}
